Alembic migrations for Doc-mate.

The database URL comes from the DATABASE_URL environment variable (see
app/core/config.py); alembic.ini's sqlalchemy.url is only a placeholder.

Common commands (run from backend/):
  alembic upgrade head        # apply all migrations
  alembic downgrade -1        # roll back one
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "message"   # needs a reachable DB

The initial migration (0001) enables the pgvector extension before creating
tables, so it must run against a Postgres instance that has pgvector available.
